# The shared DC bus: braking feeds the axes' energy back, and the diode
# bridge can't return it to the mains. With only the drives' own 1410 uF a
# fast diagonal stop lifts the bus close to the drives' 380 V trip; 10 mF
# keeps it near the mains peak (325 V); a brake chopper at 370 V clips it.
# (Very hard stops regenerate less: the ironless coils' resistance burns
# it, 1.5 R I^2.)
@program portal/portal_sim
@args portal/machine/portal.portal
run 0.05
lcnc 1
run 0.2
move 0.5 50 100
run 0.3
trapfrac 0.12
mark
tmove 0.65 950 900
run 0.3
print bus_max bus_min e_regen e_chopper fault
bus 10000 230 1.0
run 0.1
mark
tmove 0.65 50 100
run 0.3
print bus_max bus_min e_regen e_chopper fault
bus 1410 230 1.0 370 30
run 0.1
mark
tmove 0.65 950 900
run 0.3
print bus_max bus_min e_regen e_chopper fault
@expect portal.bus_max[1] > 360
@expect portal.bus_max[1] < 380
@expect portal.bus_min[1] < 300
@expect portal.e_regen[1] > 15
@expect portal.bus_max[2] < 330
@expect portal.bus_max[3] < 372
@expect portal.e_chopper[3] > 1
@expect max portal.fault == 0
@reject ^ERROR
